# `box` is proven to hold a Crate and the call by value gives `anything`: the allocation cannot list it and it is defined behind the allocation. The allocation lists note, read, add and the hidden scope of the two closures left unmade: four fields, as many as are written. That is no sign that the object is as allocated: the read of `box` and the test `in` ask the object.
